# Patch 0006 — skill: edits are plain track-edit, never linked to a comment with --thread
# Offered back: no (romp-only)
# Files: skill/SKILL.md
#
# Reason: the skill tells an agent revising in answer to a review comment to pass `track-edit
# --thread <id>`, which binds the edit to the comment so the editor folds it into the comment's
# conversation as a revision step. In this host's review loop the reviewer reads edits as changes in
# the text and words as replies, and an edit shown inside a comment instead of as its own change
# confused them (the user, 2026-09-09: the link is removed, and the review message no longer names
# it). The skill now says: make every edit with plain `track-edit`, never `--thread`, and answer a
# comment in words with `track-reply --thread <id>`. Coalescing is described as it is (a second
# edit over the same span rewrites the suggestion, which the reviewer reads as it stands). Other
# hosts keep the fold, so this is not offered back. Pinned by the drift test only (prose).
